Essential Commands to Manage Your Deployment

To apply the configuration and verify the deployment status, use the following kubectl commands: [1] (/goto?url=CAESjQEB6zswFR6z7UHKXuEah7U8MpP0A2mEqpsaY1CGuCBinp0rt-BSHhBx-KFkNPZynBdOuY_bYnNXRQv-NonNLStMZt1tsBTrj2UJAWKgeLCMG4WCYXUNs4U-UDVEf2gjBnQGULfglelz-JaDrk3SPUpStN6n6YgpXAzVwh29nwHrvHLPl6XFNY3xP50RWi4)
bash
# Apply the YAML configuration file
kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml

# Check the status of your running deployment
kubectl get deployments

# See the active pods managed by this deployment
kubectl get pods -l app=nginx

# Dynamically scale your replicas up or down
kubectl scale deployment nginx-deployment --replicas=5
